      "level": 2,
      "content": "Traffic Light Signals"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Traffic light signals regulate vehicle flow at intersections using Red (Stop), Amber/Yellow (Caution/Prepare to Stop), and Green (Go).",
        "Traffic signs are divided into three primary categories: Mandatory/Regulatory, Cautionary/Warning, and Informatory signs.",
        "Mandatory signs are generally circular (except STOP and GIVE WAY) and carry strict legal penalties if violated.",
        "Cautionary signs are triangular in shape and alert drivers to potential road hazards ahead.",
        "Road markings like solid lines, broken lines, yellow lines, and zebra crossings guide lane discipline and pedestrian safety."
      ],
      "id": "l09e3op"
    },
