    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a8mm6c1",
      "content": "<strong>Mandatory Signs (Red circle border): </strong>These signs MUST be obeyed. Ignoring them is an offence. Examples: STOP, No Entry, Speed Limit, No Parking, No U-Turn, Give Way, No Overtaking, One Way."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3gwnwtt",
      "content": "<strong>Cautionary / Warning Signs (Yellow diamond / triangle): </strong>These warn drivers of a hazard ahead. Examples: Sharp curve, Slippery road, School ahead, Speed breaker, Road narrows, Pedestrian crossing, Cattle crossing."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wyrvhj7",
      "content": "<strong>Informatory Signs (Blue rectangle): </strong>These give helpful information. Examples: Parking, Hospital, Petrol pump, First Aid Post, Bus stop, Telephone."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The STOP sign is uniquely octagonal in shape, whereas the GIVE WAY sign is an inverted triangle.",
        "A continuous solid double yellow line indicates a strict prohibition against crossing or overtaking from either side.",
        "Disregarding traffic signs and signals attracts legal penalties under Section 119 and Section 177 of the Motor Vehicles Act."
      ],
      "id": "xww7bmu"
    },
